CH = dict(num=21, tag="Economics · Ch 5", theme="Consumer exploitation, consumer movement, rights, redressal and awareness",
 title="Consumer Rights",
 intro="In a market, a buyer is often in a weaker position than the seller. Rules and organised action protect consumers. This chapter explains how consumers are exploited, how the consumer movement developed in India, the consumer rights and the redressal machinery under the Consumer Protection Act, and how an aware consumer can act.",
 big_questions=["How are consumers exploited in the marketplace?", "How did the consumer movement begin in India?", "What are the consumer rights?", "How can consumers seek redressal?", "How can consumers become aware?"],
 blocks=[
 ("h2", "The Consumer in the Marketplace"),
 ("ul", ["In markets, **consumers** are exploited in many ways: **short weights and measures**, selling at **higher than the printed price**, **adulteration**, **sale of defective goods**, **false and misleading advertisements** and poor after-sales service. Examples: a customer finds in a packet less weight than printed; harmful ingredients are hidden.", "Producers are few and powerful; individual consumers are many and scattered with less information. Consumers may also get **lured by misleading advertising**.", "The **Consumer Protection** movement and law aim at making the market fair: rules and regulations are needed to protect consumers and a way to enforce them."]),
 ("h2", "Consumer Movement in India"),
 ("ul", ["The consumer movement arose out of dissatisfaction of consumers with unfair practices of sellers: hoarding, black-marketing, adulteration of food and edible oil. The movement made progress after the **1960s**; the consumer groups wrote articles, visited ration shops and exposed them. Till the 1970s, consumer organisations were involved in writing articles and holding exhibitions.", "In **1985**, the **UN General Assembly adopted the UN Guidelines for Consumer Protection**, a tool for nations to adopt measures to protect consumers.", "In India, the **Consumer Protection Act (COPRA), 1986** was enacted after great effort by consumer groups; it set up the **three-tier quasi-judicial machinery**. The Act was replaced by the **Consumer Protection Act, 2019**, in force from **July 2020**. **National Consumer Day is observed on 24 December**, as the COPRA of 1986 was enacted on this day; **World Consumer Rights Day is on 15 March**.", "A consumer forum or association guides consumers, and may represent consumers in the consumer courts. **ISI, Agmark, Hallmark** and **ISO** are standard marks; the **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS)** develops standards."]),
 ("table", ["Mark", "Used for"], [["ISI", "Industrial products (BIS standard)"], ["Agmark", "Agricultural products such as edible oil, ghee, spices"], ["Hallmark", "Purity of gold jewellery"], ["ISO", "International standards for management and quality systems"]]),
 ("h2", "Consumer Rights"),
 ("table", ["Right", "Meaning"], [["Right to safety", "Protection against goods and services hazardous to life and property, e.g. defective electrical goods, medicines, unsafe LPG cylinders; producers must follow safety rules"], ["Right to be informed", "Details of ingredients, price, batch number, date of manufacture, expiry date and manufacturer's address; the right to get information about goods and services; **RTI Act (2005)** gives information on government services"], ["Right to choose", "Freedom to choose from a variety of goods at competitive prices; no seller may force a buyer to purchase an item in a bundle"], ["Right to represent (to be heard)", "Consumers' interests are given due consideration in the forums, and consumer groups can be heard"], ["Right to seek redressal", "Compensation against unfair trade practices and exploitation; refund, repair or replacement"], ["Right to consumer education", "Knowledge and skills to be an informed consumer throughout life"]]),
 ("h2", "Redressal: How to Get Justice"),
 ("ul", ["Under the Act of 1986 a **three-tier quasi-judicial** machinery was set up at **district, state and national** levels: the **District Forum, State Commission and National Commission**; under the 2019 Act, they are called **District, State and National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commissions (NCDRC)**. A consumer who feels cheated can file a complaint (with documents such as bill and warranty); lawyers are not mandatory.", "**Pecuniary jurisdiction (under rules of 2021):** a District Commission handles cases up to Rs 1 crore; a State Commission above Rs 1 crore up to Rs 10 crore; the National Commission above Rs 10 crore. If dissatisfied with the district order, a consumer can appeal to the State Commission and then the National Commission.", "The **Consumer Protection Act, 2019** established the **Central Consumer Protection Authority (CCPA)** to protect rights, deal with misleading advertisements and unfair trade practices, and covers **e-commerce**, product liability and mediation. A consumer can also file a complaint online.", "A consumer cannot always get redressal quickly: cases are often delayed, cost of litigation, and lack of evidence; **consumer awareness** is needed to make the movement effective."]),
 ("h2", "Becoming an Alert Consumer"),
 ("ul", ["Know your rights; **ask for a cash memo or bill** and keep the warranty card; check the **expiry date, MRP and standard marks** (ISI, Agmark, Hallmark) before buying; compare products; do not be misled by advertisements; **report** exploitation to a consumer forum.", "Consumer awareness also needs consumers to act as **responsible citizens**: avoiding waste and protecting the environment. Consumer groups, the media and the government should work together; the consumer movement is effective only if consumers are active."]),
 ("h2", "Quick Revision: Likely Exam Questions"),
 ("qa", [
  ("Why are consumers exploited?", "Poor information, scattered buyers and powerful sellers."),
  ("Name six consumer rights.", "Safety, information, choice, representation, redressal and consumer education."),
  ("When is National Consumer Day?", "24 December."),
  ("What is the three-tier machinery?", "District, State and National Commissions."),
  ("What does ISI mark show?", "Standard of quality for industrial goods, set by BIS."),
  ("What is Agmark?", "Quality mark for agricultural products."),
  ("What is the CCPA?", "Central Consumer Protection Authority under the 2019 Act."),
 ]),
 ],
 takeaways=["Consumers are exploited through **adulteration, short weights, high prices and misleading ads**.", "The consumer movement led to **COPRA 1986** and the **Consumer Protection Act 2019**.", "Six rights: **safety, information, choice, representation, redressal and education**.", "Redressal is through **District, State and National Commissions**; the **CCPA** acts on unfair practices and e-commerce.", "An alert consumer asks for bills, checks marks (**ISI, Agmark, Hallmark**) and reports malpractice."])
